# Prefills

**The workout's kg is the routine's kg** — a number the user typed or confirmed (DEC-096). The routine gets it from **history** when an exercise is added (`historyPrescription`: the picker's `pickerItem`, `RoutineExerciseNew`, a plan slot, a mid-workout replacement's first set), and from the **user's confirmed update** after an exercise (the "Update <routine>" offer, `routineUpdateOffer` → `store.applyRoutineUpdate`, that routine only). Nothing else writes it silently: Finish never does (DEC-056); History's recalculation writes only on Apply.

## The live set form (`setLogSeed` / `initialSetFields` / `setPreview`, `workout-log.js`)

A **work set's kg**, highest first:
1. an unsaved draft of this set (req-125), or the set just un-logged via Previous;
2. an in-session kg change for this exercise (req-83 / DEC-052 override);
3. **the routine kg at this set's index** (`routineKgFor` → the snapshot item's `suggestedWeights`, frozen at Start), when > 0;
4. the kg just logged this session (DEC-002 / req-152 carry), only when the routine has no kg there;
5. blank. History does **not** seed a work set's kg.

A **warm-up set's kg** stays on history (`historySetPrefill`) — the routine holds no warm-up kg. **Reps** prefill from that set's target and never carry (DEC-052). **Effort** defaults to Moderate only where Effort is shown (req-156).

## Never invented

A weighted exercise without history and without a routine kg starts blank — no invented starting weight (DEC-012). Do not invent warmup (50% load, 12 reps), rest, or notes (copy of `ex.cues`); do not prefill from recommendations, library cues or type defaults. Editing an existing record may show that record's saved values.

**One exception at routine creation (DEC-097 §4, req-180):** the Add exercise picker adds an exercise with **no history** with a **starting plan** — reps 3 × 10, 90 s rest; timed 3 × the exercise's duration, 90 s rest; cardio 1 set, rest 0 (`routine-picker.js` `pickerItem`). It is shown on the selected row ("Starting plan: … — change any time"), never silent, and **never a kg** (`suggestedWeights: []`). With history, the whole history prescription is used instead — the two are never mixed.

**The one-time fill (req-178, DEC-096 §6 / DEC-100):** on the first load of this build, each routine item's kg is set from latest history where history has a kg (`routine-kg-fill.js`, marker `routineKgFilledAt`), so the next workout reads as it did when history seeded it. It runs once per stored state, never on a blank device.
